<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fort Zeelandia (Guyana)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">18th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fort Zeelandia is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> brick fort on Fort Island in the mouth of the Essequibo River in Guyana. Built in the 18th century, it replaced the older stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyk-over-al">Kyk-over-al</a> as the seat of the Dutch colony of Essequibo, housing the commander and the colony's governing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/court-of-policy">Court of Policy</a>. The fort and the nearby Court of Policy hall survive and are kept as heritage sites.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fort-zeelandia-guyana.jpg" alt="Fort Zeelandia (Guyana)" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: C. van Henemann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vlaggeneiland-Fort-Zeelandia-Essequebo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
